> I’d structure this as a small, layered package so the initial synchronous selector can evolve into a durable DAG/workflow system without breaking the existing `Planner` API.
> 
> ```text
> planner/
> ├── __init__.py                 # Public exports: Planner, Response, StreamResponse, etc.
> ├── planner.py                  # Main synchronous facade / compatibility API
> ├── types.py                    # Shared dataclasses and protocols
> ├── registry.py                 # Versioned model/tool/plan registration
> ├── responders.py               # Responder protocol and concrete plan responders
> ├── plans.py                    # Plan templates, PlanSpec, configured tool variants
> ├── selection.py                # Policy interface + BayesSelector adapter
