> 3. **Context assembly**
>    - Keep canonical messages immutable.
>    - Build effective messages per selected plan.
>    - Attach injected material with provenance and token-budget rules.
> 
> 4. **Durable persistence**
>    - Define repository protocols first.
>    - Implement `InMemoryRepository`; later add SQLite/Postgres without changing planner logic.
> 
> 5. **Workflow/DAG layer**
>    - Introduce operations, artifacts, event log, reducer, and scheduler.
>    - Initially execute synchronously; later attach worker queues.
>    - Keep `poll()` as the stable external delivery mechanism.
> 
> The immediate first coding target should be `types.py`, `registry.py`, `responders.py`, `selection.py`, `persistence.py`, and a rewritten `planner.py`. This gives you a useful, testable plan-selection system before introducing workflow infrastructure.
