> ### `planner/tools/calculator.py`
> 
> ```python
> """
> Safe calculator tool.
> 
> The calculator evaluates only a restricted mathematical expression language.
> It must use AST parsing with an explicit allowlist of node types, operators,
> functions, constants, numeric limits, and execution-time limits. It must not
> use unrestricted eval(), import access, attribute access, indexing into
> arbitrary objects, file access, or function calls outside the allowlist.
> 
> Exports legacy-compatible registration metadata:
> 
> calculator_info = {
>     "name": "calculator",
>     "description": "...",
>     "fn": calculate,
>     "config": {...},
>     "quality_prior": ...,
>     "cost_estimate": ...,
> }
> 
> Expected helper:
>     def calculate(invocation: ToolInvocation) -> ToolResult: ...
> 
> Caller:
>     Planner.register_tool(**calculate_tool.calculator_info)
> 
> The result should contain the numerical answer, normalized expression,
> calculation provenance, and any warnings about invalid/unsafe input.
> """
> ```
> 
> ---
> 
> ### `planner/tools/memory.py` and `planner/tools/search.py`
> 
> ```python
> """
> Typed retrieval/search tool implementation.
> 
> Memory/search configuration is a first-class decision variable, including:
> collection(s), filters, top-k, score threshold, reranking strategy, token
> budget, summarization strategy, recency limits, source whitelists, extraction
> depth, and review-only/source-quality filters.
> 
> Required behavior:
> - return retrieved records and exact excerpts as typed Artifacts;
> - include provenance, timestamps, source URLs/identifiers, and trust level;
> - label retrieved content as potentially stale and externally supplied;
> - treat retrieved documents as untrusted data, never as privileged
>   instructions;
> - produce concise context candidates rather than injecting arbitrary raw text.
> 
> Expected helper:
>     def retrieve(invocation: ToolInvocation) -> ToolResult: ...
> or:
>     def search(invocation: ToolInvocation) -> ToolResult: ...
> 
> Caller:
> - plans.py creates bounded discrete configuration variants;
> - responders.py/workflow.workers invokes the tool;
> - context.py chooses eligible excerpts under a token and relevance budget.
> """
> ```
