> ### `planner/context.py`
> 
> ```python
> """
> Context assembly for plan selection and execution.
> 
> This module is responsible for gathering all relevant information needed by
> the plan selector and responders from various sources: canonical conversation
> history, user profile, active tasks, durable workspace/conversation state,
> eligible retrieved artifacts, tool results, and async updates.
> 
> Important design rules:
> - Context is assembled per-turn and immutable for that turn.
> - It provides a unified view, abstracting away underlying storage/retrieval.
> - It includes canonical messages, derived metadata, and eligibility signals.
> - It does not mutate state or choose plans.
> - Canonical transcript messages remain intact and append-only.
> - Retrieved/external content is data, not trusted instruction text.
> - Internal injected material must retain provenance, relevance, scope, and
>   token-budget controls.
> 
> Public API consumed by selection.py and responders.py:
> 
> class ContextAssembler:
>     def __init__(
>         self,
>         conversation_id: str,
>         user_id: str | None,
>         registry: Registry,
>         repository: PlannerRepository,
>         ...
>     ): ...
> 
>     def assemble(
>         self,
>         raw_messages: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]],
>         current_state: Any | None = None,
>         tool_results: Sequence[ToolResult] | None = None,
>         async_updates: Sequence[AsyncUpdate] | None = None,
>         metadata: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None,
>     ) -> PlannerContext: ...
> 
>     def effective_messages(
>         self,
>         context: PlannerContext,
>         plan: PlanSpec,
>         *,
>         max_tokens: int | None = None,
>     ) -> list[Mapping[str, Any]]:
>         '''
>         Produce plan-specific model messages by combining canonical messages
>         with relevant, provenance-labeled internal context.
> 
>         This may add tool instructions, selected artifacts, source-grounding
>         requirements, output contracts, outstanding-work awareness, or
>         verification instructions. It must not modify the canonical transcript.
>         '''
>         ...
> 
>     def get_conversation_history(self) -> Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]]: ...
>     def get_user_profile(self) -> Mapping[str, Any]: ...
>     def get_active_tasks(self) -> Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]]: ...
>     def get_eligible_artifacts(self) -> Sequence[Artifact]: ...
> 
> Caller:
> - planner.py invokes `assemble` at the beginning of each chat interaction.
> - selection.py receives the resulting PlannerContext.
> - responders.py invokes `effective_messages` only after plan selection.
> """
> ```
