> 
> ### `planner/async_api.py`
> 
> ```python
> """
> Synchronous facade for internally asynchronous work.
> 
> Initial implementation is intentionally inert:
> 
>     poll() -> []
>     ongoing() -> []
>     async_status() -> {"count": 0, "operations": []}
> 
> Later it exposes durable workflow results without requiring application callers
> to become async.
> 
> Public API:
> 
> class AsyncWorkService:
>     def poll(self, conversation_id: str) -> list[AsyncUpdate]: ...
>     def ongoing(self, conversation_id: str) -> list[OperationSummary]: ...
>     def async_status(self, conversation_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]: ...
> 
> Caller:
> - planner.py delegates Planner.poll/ongoing/async_status here.
> - workflow/delivery.py writes eligible delivered updates.
> """
> ```
